int main() {
    //Switch on string — NLang supports string in switch discriminators.
    //Mechanism note (pre-Phase-12-Step-1): labels compare by string-pool
    //index (OP_Equal_i32 on interned literals), NOT string content —
    //equal literals share one pool entry so they match; computed strings
    //("hel"+"lo") would fall to default. Step 1 changes this to value
    //comparison (OP_Eq_str). Verifies the early "hi" case fails, the
    //"hello" case matches.
    string s = "hello";
    switch (s) {
        case "hi": return 1;
        case "hello": return 2;
        default: return 0;
    }
}
